// Generated by scripts/gen-lab-bundle.mjs from lab-guide/clab. Pages not listed here fall back to lab-markdown.ts.
export const LAB_MARKDOWN_CLAB: Record<string, string> = {
    "/exercises/fundamentals": "---\nicon: atom\n---\n\n# Install Lab Dependencies\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n\nThis contains critical steps to prepare your Demo Hub Instance.\n\n1.  Ensure you are at least in Zurich Patch 6. Go to **All** > type **stats.do** and hit Return/Enter ↵. Ensure that it is empty.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_fund_stats.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  You should get a build tag with Zurich and the needed patch name.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_demohub_stats_build_tag.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3. If you have not done so yet, log in to [Demo Hub](https://demohub.service-now.com/) then go to the [APAC End-to-End AI Workshop ](https://demohub.service-now.com/edsp?id=sc_cat_item\\&sys_id=8bb12066fb2f761042e1f57675efdc85\\&sysparm_category=f2d15f6893429250e0d5b3aa6aba105a)catalog item to install the lab dependencies in your instance.\n4.  Provide your <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> Zurich Patch 6 or newer **Instance** name, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Admin User ID**, and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Password**, then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Submit**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_fund_cat_item.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"516\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5. Wait for 10 to 15 minutes.\n6. Once completed, you will get an email indicating that the import of update sets is successful.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_fund_cat_complete.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n## Next step\n\nLet us continue building the data foundations for the use case. Next up is creation of the Data Fabric tables which will be used by AI Agents. Let us work on AI Agents' ability to use REST API connectivity by proceeding with the [Integration Hub configuration](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/main-exercises/lab-exercise-integration-hub).\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n",
    "/exercises/integration-hub": "---\nicon: link\n---\n\n# Lab Exercise: Integration Hub\n\n## Where we are in this workshop\n\n<figure><picture><source srcset=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_integration_hub_dark.png\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_integration_hub.png\" alt=\"Integration Hub focus: Expense to REST API\"></picture><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n> **Legend:** 🟤 Data | 🟣 Workflow Data Fabric | 🔵 External Systems | ↓ Takes data from\n\n## Lab Exercise: Integration Hub\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n\nIn this lab you use **Build Agent** to build, in the **Forecast Variance** app, the **Action**, **Subflows** and **AI agent** that get expense data from an external REST API, check the cost center against its budget, and create a Finance case when the cost center will be over budget.\n\nThe tables and their data are already in the app. You build the logic on top of them with four prompts, then run it and watch the agent react.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_inthub_overview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_inthub_demo_preview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### Lab Sections and Objectives\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#data-flow\">1</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Context Setting:</strong> Review the data flow diagram. Understand how ServiceNow consumes a REST API endpoint, writes the events to a scoped table, triggers an AI Agent, and creates a Finance Case automatically.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**Preparation**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#preparation-platform-configuration\">2</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Platform Configuration:</strong> Set the AI model provider, the scope and the <code>sn_aia.admin</code> role.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#preparation-initial-checks\">3</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Initial Check:</strong> Verify the Now Assist panel is accessible.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**Build with Build Agent**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#hands-on-expense-event-integration\">4</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Expense Event Integration:</strong> Build Agent creates the \"Get Expense Event\" alias, action and subflow, and tests them.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#hands-on-budget-check-subflows\">5</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Budget Check Subflows:</strong> Build Agent creates the \"Extract Cost Center\" and \"Budget Variance Analysis\" subflows, and tests them.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#hands-on-forecast-variance-ai-agent\">6</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>AI Agent:</strong> Build Agent creates the \"Forecast Variance\" agent with your initials after the name, its four tools and its trigger.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**AI Agent and Finance Operations Workspace**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#hands-on-flow-execution\">7</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Run the Flow:</strong> Empty the Expense Transaction Event table, then run the \"Get Expense Event\" subflow.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#walkthrough-agent-runtime\">8</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Watch the AI Agent React:</strong> Open Now Assist. Explore the steps the agent ran, the cost center and vendor history, the budget analysis and the Finance Case link.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#completion-verify-finance-case\">9</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Verify the Finance Case:</strong> Find the case created by the agent in Finance Operations Workspace.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-integration-hub.md#conclusion\">10</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Walk through the complete data flow chain. An external event triggers proactive financial intelligence with zero human intervention.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n### Data flow\n\nThe data flow below shows how ServiceNow consumes the REST API endpoint through an Integration Hub connection alias and action. The subflow writes the entries to the scoped table, and each new entry triggers the AI agent, which checks the cost center against Cost Center Budget History.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"User Interaction Layer\"\n        Employee((Employee/<br/>Finance Manager))\n        EC[Employee Center or<br/> Workspace with Now Assist]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"External Systems\"\n        ExpenseAPI[Expense Event<br/>API]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"ServiceNow AI Platform\"\n        subgraph \"Data Integration Layer\"\n            IntHub[Integration Hub<br/>Alias, Action, Subflow]\n        end\n\n        subgraph \"ServiceNow Native Tables\"\n            ExpenseTable[(Expense Event<br/>Line Items<br/>Scoped Table)]\n            BudgetTable[(Cost Center<br/>Budget History<br/>Scoped Table)]\n            FinCase[(Finance Case<br/>Table)]\n        end\n\n        subgraph \"AI & Automation\"\n            Agent2[Agent: Forecast<br/>Variance]\n            Lookups[Record Lookups]\n            FlowAction[Subflows]\n        end\n    end\n\n    %% Data Flow Connections\n    ExpenseAPI -->|Real-time Events| IntHub\n    IntHub -->|Write| ExpenseTable\n\n    %% Agent Workflow\n    ExpenseTable -->|Incoming Event| Agent2\n    BudgetTable -->|Current Budget| Agent2\n    Agent2 <-->|Cost Center and<br/>Vendor History| Lookups\n    Agent2 <-->|Extract Cost Center,<br/>Budget Variance Analysis| FlowAction\n    FlowAction -->|Create Case| FinCase\n\n    %% User Interaction Connections\n    Employee -->|Ask Questions<br/>View/Update Cases| EC\n    EC -->|Search & Query| FinCase\n\n    %% Styling\n    classDef external fill:#2196F3,stroke:#1565C0,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n    classDef user fill:#F5F5F5,stroke:#616161,stroke-width:3px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef nowassist fill:#FFB300,stroke:#F57F17,stroke-width:2px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef platform fill:#4CAF50,stroke:#2E7D32,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n    classDef wdf fill:#9C27B0,stroke:#6A1B9A,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n\n    class ExpenseAPI external\n    class IntHub wdf\n    class ExpenseTable,BudgetTable,FinCase platform\n    class Agent2,Lookups nowassist\n    class FlowAction platform\n    class Employee,EC user\n```\n\n> **Color Legend:** 🟡 Now Assist | 🟢 Platform | 🟣 Workflow Data Fabric | 🔵 External Systems | ⚪ User Interaction\n>\n> [📊 View High-Resolution Diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/dataflow_integration_hub.png)\n\n### Preparation\n\n#### Preparation: LLM Configuration\n\nEnsure the **AI model provider** is **Azure OpenAI** to so you have an experience consistent to the environment in which the lab has been built on.&#x20;\n\n1.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **AI Admin Hub** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Settings**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/image.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"337\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> Manage AI models > Manage model providers then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click the **Model providers** tab (takes \\~2 minutes to load) and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> check whether the **Default model provider** column is <mark style=\"color:red;\">**NOT**</mark> **Azure OpenAI** (e.g. **AWS Claude** or **Now LLM Service**). If it is NOT Azure OpenAI, click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> **Edit model provider** (top right); else, skip to section **Preparation: Platform Configuration**. When you click **Edit model provider**, the screen will refresh and change its layout.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/image (1).png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  In the drop-down, select <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Azure OpenAI** then click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Save and Activate**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/image (2).png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  It will take \\~3-5 minutes to reassign the services. This will result in the screen below. There might be services which will not be assigned successfully, and this can be ignored (e.g. in screenshot below there are 35 skills that failed reassignment to Azure OpenAI. Click **Okay**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/image (3).png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  Finally the **Model provider** column will show that the assignment is mostly **Azure OpenAI**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/image (4).png\" alt=\"\" width=\"563\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Preparation: Platform Configuration\n\nThese are required preparation steps in platform level. These are cross configurations that affect instance behaviour (across applications).\n\n1. As **admin** user, this preparation section includes setting up of the scope, authorisation and Now Assist configurations.\n2.  Ensure you are in the correct scope. Click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **scope** (globe icon) and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Forecast Variance**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_fund_exercise_scope.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Users and Groups** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Users and Groups > Users**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_agent_studio_users_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  Search for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **System Administrator** then hit **Return/Enter ↵** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **admin**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_search_admin_user.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  In the **Roles** tab, click **Edit...** (on this build the button reads **Edit...**). If a **Say hello to ServiceNow Otto** dialog appears on first load, click **Got it**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_roles_tab_edit.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n6.  Search for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **sn\\_aia.admin** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **sn\\_aia.admin** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click on **>** to move the role to the right panel > then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Save**. You will notice that there are also roles for integration and viewer purposes which can be assigned for users who will need less privileges.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_roles_sn_aia_save.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n7.  Right-click on the top panel and click **Save**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_xcc_prep_save.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n8.  <mark style=\"color:red;\">**IMPORTANT**</mark>. Log out and log back in.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_logout.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"254\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Preparation: Allow the AI agent to call the subflows (Invoked from AI ACLs)\n\n<mark style=\"color:red;\">**IMPORTANT for lab.service-now.com instances (Brazil and later).**</mark> These builds deny an AI agent access to any subflow tool unless an **Invoked from AI** access control exists for that subflow. Without it the agent test stops at **Access verification** with **Access denied** on the tool and the answer **You don't have the required access to complete this request**. The Forecast Variance subflows do not ship with these ACLs, so create the two below once per instance. The two Search tools and the agent itself need nothing.\n\n1. As **admin**, open the user menu (your avatar, top right) > **Elevate role** > tick **security\\_admin** > **Update**. The ACL form is read-only without this.\n2. Go to **All** > type **Access Controls** (`sys_security_acl_list.do`) > click **New**.\n3. Set **Type** to **flow**. **Operation** fills in as **invoke\\_from\\_ai**. **Decision Type** stays **Allow If**. **Application** reads **Forecast Variance**.\n4. In **Name**, enter the scope-qualified internal name of the subflow. Use the table below. The internal name is not the display name, and the form accepts any text, so a wrong name saves without an error and the tool stays denied.\n\n   | Agent tool | Subflow | Name to enter |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | Budget Variance Analysis | Budget Variance Analysis | `x_snc_forecast_v_0.budget_variance_analysis` |\n   | Extract Cost Center | Extract Cost Center | `x_snc_forecast_v_0.cost_center_history` |\n\n   To check an internal name: All > **Flows** list, filter on **Internal name**.\n5. Click **Submit**. The role cannot be added on the new-record form, so open the ACL again.\n6. In **Requires role**, double-click **Insert a new row...**, type **admin**, pick **admin** from the list, click the green tick, then click **Update** on the ACL. Check that the role shows in the list.\n7. Repeat steps 2 to 6 for the second subflow.\n\nYou will test the result in **Walkthrough: Agent Runtime**: every tool should show **Completed** in the AI agent decision logs.\n\n#### Preparation: Initial Checks\n\nVerify the Now Assist panel is accessible.\n\n1.  If you have set up the Now Assist Panel correctly, you should see the Otto/sparkle icon on the top right.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_now_assist_panel.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. If the Otto/sparkle icon is missing, or the **Testing** tab of AI Agent Studio shows a banner about the assistant, two instance settings are off on lab.service-now.com builds. Turn them on once:\n   - **All** > **AI Admin Hub** > **ServiceNow Otto panel** > **Turn on**.\n   - **All** > **Assistant Designer** > **ServiceNow Otto panel - Platform (default)** > **Activate** (the Testing banner links to it).\n3. To test the agent directly, go to AI Agent Studio > **Testing** > **Manual Test** > **AI agent or workflow**, pick **Forecast Variance Integration Hub Trigger** and send **Help me process EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01**. The decision log lists **Access verification** and then each tool, all showing **Completed** once the **Invoked from AI** ACLs from the platform preparation exist.\n\n### Build with Build Agent\n\n> **Using Build Agent:** go to ServiceNow Studio, open the **Forecast Variance** app, click **Build Agent** (diamond icon) > **New conversation**, then paste the prompt. Build Agent shows each script before running it; click **Approve**. If it asks you a question, answer it in the chat. If you see a 401 error, reload the page and send the prompt again. Start a new conversation for each prompt.\n\n<figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_ba_new_conversation.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: Expense Event Integration\n\nBuild Agent creates the connection to the expense API, the **Action** that reads it, and the **Subflow** that runs the action.\n\n1.  Paste this prompt and send it.\n\n    ```\n    In the Forecast Variance app:\n    1. Create a connection and credential alias named \"Get Expense Event\", with an HTTP\n    connection to https://wdflab.servicenow.workers.dev.\n    2. Create a Flow Designer action named \"Get Expense Event\" that sends GET\n    /api/expense-events through that alias. For each returned event whose Event ID isn't\n    already in the Expense Transaction Event table, the action itself creates an Expense\n    Transaction Event record, copying each field with the same name and setting Owner to the\n    user running it. amount_usd arrives as text with commas, so remove them.\n    3. Create a subflow named \"Get Expense Event\" that only runs that action, as the user who\n    starts it.\n    Then build and install the app, and test it by running the subflow once.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve** each time Build Agent asks. When it finishes, you should see the **Get Expense Event** alias, action and subflow installed, and the test adding the event **EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01** to the Expense Transaction Event table. The first run of the action grants itself about ten cross-scope privileges (for example for REST messages, connection aliases and Finance Case); this is expected for a scoped app and needs no action from you.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_ihub_ba_result_1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: Budget Check Subflows\n\nBuild Agent creates the two subflows the agent uses as tools, plus the **Compute Budget Totals** action that does the budget math. **Budget Variance Analysis** is the deterministic part: it adds the new expense to the cost center's 2025 actual spend and creates a Finance Case when the total is over budget.\n\n1.  In a new conversation, paste this prompt and send it.\n\n    ```\n    In the Forecast Variance app:\n    1. Create a subflow named \"Extract Cost Center\" with input Event ID (string). It looks up\n    the Expense Transaction Event record with that Event ID and outputs its Cost Center and\n    Vendor.\n    2. Create a Flow Designer action named \"Compute Budget Totals\" with inputs Cost Center\n    and Event ID (strings). Its script step looks up the Expense Transaction Event with that\n    Event ID, totals Monthly Budget and Actual Spend for that cost center in Cost Center\n    Budget History for fiscal year 2025 (add the records up one by one, because\n    GlideAggregate SUM is wrong on these currency fields), and adds the event's amount_usd\n    to the actual. It outputs Over Budget, the new actual, the short description \"<cost\n    center> is exceeding budget\" and the cost center's Owner, declared as a String output\n    that holds the owner's sys_id (not a reference field). Keep this code in the action,\n    because a subflow's own scripts can't read the subflow's inputs.\n    3. Create a subflow named \"Budget Variance Analysis\" with inputs Cost Center and Event ID\n    (strings). It runs Compute Budget Totals. If Over Budget is true, it creates a Finance\n    Case (sn_spend_sdc_service_request) with that short description, assigned to the Owner,\n    and outputs \"<case number> - <short description>\". Otherwise it outputs \"Cost center is\n    compliant with budget.\" Also output the new actual as Sum.\n    Then build and install the app. To test, run Extract Cost Center with event ID\n    EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01, then run Budget Variance Analysis with cost center PROD-DE-2\n    and that event ID, so no Finance Case is created.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve** each time Build Agent asks. You should see **Extract Cost Center** return **CC_IT_001** and **Amazon Web Services**, and **Budget Variance Analysis** return **Cost center is compliant with budget.** with a Sum of **109200.75** for PROD-DE-2.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_ihub_ba_result_2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: Forecast Variance AI Agent\n\nBuild Agent creates the **AI agent**, its tools and the trigger that starts it when a new expense event arrives.\n\n1.  In a new conversation, paste this prompt, replace **\\<your initials>** with your initials (for example **LF**) and send it.\n\n    ```\n    In the Forecast Variance app, create an AI agent named \"Forecast Variance <your initials>\"\n    that reviews new expense events and opens a Finance Case when a cost center goes over\n    budget. Its tools run without asking:\n    - the \"Extract Cost Center\" subflow\n    - the \"Budget Variance Analysis\" subflow\n    - \"Search for Cost Center History\": looks up up to 12 Cost Center Budget History\n    records by cost center, ordered by fiscal month, and returns fiscal month, monthly\n    budget, actual spend and status\n    - \"Search for Expense Transactions History\": looks up records in the global table\n    x_snc_forecast_v_0_expense_transactions by cost center and vendor and returns expense\n    date, amount and description\n    Instructions:\n    1. Run Extract Cost Center with the event ID.\n    2. Run Search for Cost Center History with that cost center and say whether the months are\n    mostly On Target, Over Budget or Under Budget.\n    3. Run Search for Expense Transactions History with the cost center and vendor and say\n    whether this vendor has transacted before.\n    4. Run Budget Variance Analysis with the cost center and event ID and report its result,\n    including the Finance Case number if one was created.\n    Only users with the admin role can run it, and it uses the admin role for data access. Add\n    a trigger: when an Expense Transaction Event is created and Vendor is not empty, run as\n    the user admin (System Administrator), objective \"Review expense event ${event_id}\",\n    channel \"Now Assist Panel\" (the sys_cs_channel record of that name), trigger on.\n    Build and install the app without creating test records. An install doesn't build the\n    trigger's flow, so then re-save the trigger configuration with a GlideRecord update in\n    global scope (setForceUpdate(true), no field changes) and show the trigger_flow it gets.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve** each time Build Agent asks. You should see the agent with its four tools installed, and a **trigger_flow** named like **Expense Transaction Event - AI Agent: Forecast Variance \\<your initials>**. Without that flow the trigger never fires.\n\n#### Walkthrough: What Build Agent Built\n\nOptional. Open the records Build Agent created to see how they fit together.\n\n1. **AI Agent Studio** > **Agentic Solutions** > **AI agents** > **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** ([open the list](/sn_aia_agent_list.do?sysparm_query=nameLIKEForecast%20Variance)), then click the **Edit** pencil on the agent. **Definitions** holds the four instructions, **Tools** lists the two subflows and two record lookups, and **Access rules** shows the admin role. **Triggers** shows the trigger on the Expense Transaction Event table.\n2. **Flow Designer** > **Subflows** > **Budget Variance Analysis** ([open the list](/sys_hub_flow_list.do?sysparm_query=name=Budget%20Variance%20Analysis)). The subflow calls the **Compute Budget Totals** action, then creates the Finance Case only when the cost center is over budget.\n3. **Flow Designer** > **Actions** > **Get Expense Event** ([open the list](/sys_hub_action_type_definition_list.do?sysparm_query=name=Get%20Expense%20Event)). The script step reads the connection from the **Get Expense Event** alias, calls the API and writes the records.\n\n### Without Build Agent (manual route)\n\nUse this route when Build Agent is not available. It uses the **Get Expense Event** alias, action and subflows and the **Forecast Variance Integration Hub Trigger** agent that come with the Forecast Variance app, so no prompts are needed. Do these sections, then continue with **Walkthrough: Agent Runtime**.\n\n#### Manual: Connection Setup\n\nNavigate to Connection & Credential Aliases. Open the pre-configured \"Get Expense Event\" alias. Create a new Connection pointing to the REST API endpoint.\n\n1.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Connection & Credential Aliases** then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Connections & Credentials > Connection & Credential Aliases**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_conn_cred_aliases_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Search for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark>**&#x20;Get Expense Even**t then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Get Expense Event**. This is a pre-configured alias to reduce the rewiring needed for this lab exercise.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_search_get_expense_event.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  In the next screen, navigate to **Connections** > **New**. In this alias, we are creating a new connection which will get data from the REST API endpoint and serve as trigger for our AI Agent.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_connections_new.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  Provide <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Name** as **Get Expense Event**, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Connection URL** as [**https://wdflab.servicenow.workers.dev**](https://wdflab.servicenow.workers.dev) then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click **Submit**. The structure of the table in [Lab Exercise: Fundamentals](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-fundamentals) is based on the data coming from this REST API endpoint. The data from this endpoint will be written into the scoped table through a scoped **Action**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_connection_url_submit.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n#### Manual walkthrough: Custom Forecast Variance AI Agent\n\nThis is a walk through of how an AI agent equipped with both deterministic and probabilistic capabilities can automate research and validation of cost center history and expenses; as well as creation of Finance Cases should cost centers be above their budget allocations. <mark style=\"color:red;\">**Note:**</mark> this is a custom AI agent pre-configured in the lab instance provided in ServiceNow-led lab sessions; this is not an OOTB agent.\n\nFor this section: Open AI Agent Studio > Forecast Variance Integration Hub Trigger. Explore: Define the specialty (plain English instructions), Add tools (Search retrievals + Subflows), Define security controls (Dynamic user + admin role).\n\n1. Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **AI Agent Studio** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Create and Manage**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_agent_studio_create_manage.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2.  This will go to the list of Agentic workflows and AI agents. Go to **AI agents** tab > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> click **Conditions** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> select **Field** as **Name** <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Operator** as **is** and for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> Value type **Forecast Variance** **Integration Hub Trigger** and hit **Return/Enter ↵**. Click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**e.)**</mark> result.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_ai_studio_search.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3. Click on **Define the specialty**. This shows all the instructions for this AI Agent created in plain English. The **List of steps** describes the sequence, purpose, and nuances of the tools configured, which are shown in the next section. No further action is required in this section.&#x20;\n\n<mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**In case you have issues with Now Assist with Extract Cost Center step later:**</mark> You may need to refine step 1 with instructions along the lines of (and feel free to make adjustments): 1. **When a new entry is created in x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_expense\\_transaction\\_event, you look up the cost center using \"Extract Cost Center\" tool. This is done by using the event ID which has a format that starts with EXP, something like EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01.**\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_define_specialty.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. Next, click on **Add tools and information**. This is a collection of **Search retrievals** and **Subflows** that are used by the agent. The purpose and sequence of these tools are also described in the section **Define the specialty**. No further action is required in this section but feel free to explore the configurations of each of the tools. Below is a brief description of the tools configured for this agent:\n\n**a.) Extract Event ID:** Gets the event ID from the Expense Transaction Event table (x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_expense\\_transaction\\_event) from the entry created by the action Get Expense event (via REST).\n\n**b.) Extract Cost Center:** gets the cost center from the expense event that is written into the Expense Transaction Event table (x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_expense\\_transaction\\_event).\n\n**c.) Search Cost Center History:** a RAG based tool which gets the history of a cost center; i.e., is the cost center frequently exceeding its budget? Output serves as reference for the Finance team without the need pull out data for themselves or opening requests to data teams.\n\n**d.) Search for Expense Transactions History:** a RAG based tools which gets the expenses/invoices from a cost center to provide even more granular detail. Output serves as reference for the Finance team without the need pull out data for themselves or opening requests to data teams.\n\n**e). Budget Variance Analysis:** a deterministic flow that assesses whether the latest expense event caused the relevant cost center to be over-budget; if over-budget, creates a Finance Case.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_add_tools_info.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5. Under **Define security controls** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> click **Define data access** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> select **Dynamic user** from the drop down then > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> add the role named exactly **admin** (description *The System Administrator role*) as the **Approved role** if the field is not filled out yet. On the agents that ship with the app this field arrives empty and **Save and continue** stays disabled until it is set. The picker lists many roles ending in `_admin`, so do not pick `x_snc_forecast_v_0.admin`. For this exercise we are using permissive authorisations but this is where you can tighten authorisations for your agents allowing mechanisms such as inheriting the authorisations of logged in user (Dynamic identity type) or a predefined set of access (AI User identity type).\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_define_security.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n#### Manual: Configure AI Agent Trigger\n\nDelete any existing trigger. Create new trigger: Table = Expense Transaction Event, Field = Vendor, Condition = is not empty. Toggle trigger ON. Save.\n\n1. Next, click on **Define trigger**, which is a key part of this exercise.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_define_trigger_view.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. <mark style=\"color:red;\">**\\[IMPORTANT STEP]**</mark> Due to a bug related to the update set for this lab, if there is an existing trigger, you will need to delete that and **re-create**. Click the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **delete** icon then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Add trigger**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_trigger_delete_add.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Enter the details below for the trigger. These are basic information to identify your trigger. When the parameters in the trigger are satisfied, this will fire off the AI agent.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Select trigger**: **Created**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Name**: **Create New Expense Transaction Event \\<YOUR INITIALS>**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Trigger**: toggle **ON**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> Scroll down\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_trigger_details_1.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. More details to add below before finally saving the trigger configuration. These configurations include the target table and field and condition that needs to be satisfied to fire off the trigger, as well as logging.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Table**: **Expense Transaction Event**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Field**: **Vendor**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Condition** > **Operator**: **is not empty**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> **Sys\\_user**: **Owner**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**e.)**</mark> **Save**\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_trigger_details_2.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5. Click **Save and Continue**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_save_and_continue (1).png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n6. Finally, click on <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Select channels and status**. This configures the availability of the AI agent. In this case, it is enabled and can be accessed using <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Now Assist panel** toggled on as well as via <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark>**&#x20;Now Assist in Virtual Agent** added as chat assistant. Make sure your configuration is set as below. Once done, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Save**. <mark style=\"color:green;\">**Keep this browser window open! You will need again it later**</mark>.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_select_channels.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n#### Manual walkthrough: Action\n\nThe scoped **Action** is a key feature for the trigger that obtains expense data via REST API. If you wish to learn more on how Flows and AI Agents can get more granular and higher throughput of data through streaming, have a look at the bonus exercise on [Stream Connect for Apache Kafka](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-kafka_stream_connect).\n\nFor this section: Open Flow Designer > Action > Get Expense Event to get an idea how Actions are configured and to understand their dependencies with [Connections](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/main-exercises/lab-exercise-integration-hub#hands-on-connection-setup).\n\nThis action will populate the expense events coming from the external API endpoint we just configured.\n\n1.  Navigate to All > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Flow Designer** and go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Process Automation** > **Flow Designer**. This will open the app in a new tab.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_flow_designer_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  In the new **Flow Designer** tab that just opened, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> click **Actions** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **more (vertical three dots)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> type **Get Expense Event** then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Apply**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_action_search.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Click on Get **Expense Event**. <mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**Note:**</mark> this might take a while to load.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_action_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  In this current version of the lab, we will walk you through the components. Click on <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Get Expense Event**. The <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Base URL** here is coming from a service that creates the expense event and the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Imported Specifications** are also generated from the same service. No further action is needed in this section.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_action_details.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  Got to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Outputs** where <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **output** is generated based on the Imported Specifications. This makes the table structure in [Lab Exercise: Fundamentals](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-fundamentals) critical as missing or mismatched fields will cause this **Action** to fail in getting data from the REST endpoint.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_action_output.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n6. You now have familiarity of the **Action** used by the **Subflow** needed to trigger the **AI agent**, which is described in the next section.\n\n#### Manual: Flow Execution\n\nIn the same window of Flow Designer > Subflows > Get Expense Event. Click Test > Run Test. Wait for completion. Click execution details link. Verify all steps show Completed or Evaluated - True.\n\n1.  In a **current browser window**, click Workflow Studio to go back to the application home.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_home.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2. In the new **Flow Designer** tab that just opened, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> click **Subflows** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **more (vertical three dots)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> type Get Expense Event then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Apply**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_flow_search.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"563\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. This will lead to the subflow below. We will not cover the build of this **Flow** in detail in this lab exercise. The key thing to note is that it makes use of the **Action** also called **Get Expense Event** to update the **Transaction Event Record** table which is critical for the automation.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_get_expense_event.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"563\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. On the top right corner of the same **Subflow** screen, click **Test**. This will run an actual execution of the **Get Expense Event** subflow and get the data from the REST API endpoint we created earlier.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_test_flow.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"355\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5. A pop-up will appear. Click **Run Test**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_test_run.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"563\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n6. After a few seconds, a link which states **Your test has finished running. View the subflow execution details.** - click on it.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_test_link.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"563\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n7. If everything is working as expected, all the steps would be either <mark style=\"color:green;\">**Completed**</mark> or <mark style=\"color:green;\">**Evaluated - True**</mark>.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_test_results.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### AI Agent and Finance Operations Workspace\n\n#### Hands-on: Flow Execution\n\nThe agent reacts to new expense events, so remove the test event first and let the subflow create it again.\n\n1.  Ensure you are in the correct scope. Click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **scope** (globe icon) and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Forecast Variance**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_fund_exercise_scope.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Go to **All** > type **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_expense\\_transaction\\_event.list** and hit **Return/Enter ↵**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_expense_event_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  If the list is **NOT** empty, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> click on all the items by clicking the **top-rightmost check box** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Action on selected rows...** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click **Delete** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Delete** again.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_expense_event_delete.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  In a Build Agent conversation, paste this prompt and send it, then click **Approve**.\n\n    ```\n    Run the Forecast Variance subflow \"Get Expense Event\" once in the foreground, then show\n    the Expense Transaction Event record it created.\n    ```\n5.  You should see the event **EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01** for cost center **CC_IT_001** with you as the Owner. The new record fires the agent trigger, so carry on with **Walkthrough: Agent Runtime**.\n\n#### Walkthrough: Agent Runtime\n\nLook for the Now Assist badge. Open Now Assist chat. Expand to Modal view. Explore: the steps the agent ran, the cost center and vendor history, the budget analysis and the Finance Case link.\n\n1. Look at the top right of any ServiceNow page. You will notice that there is a new **Now Assist badge**. This is the AI agent at work in the back end because the **Get Expense Event** subflow has created a record in the **Expense Transaction Event** table. Click on the **Otto/sparkle icon** with the updated badge count. <mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**Note:**</mark> if the **Now Assist badge** does not appear, simply reload your page. <mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**In some cases the badge won't load at all**</mark> so simply open Now Assist and look for new chats/correspondences. The agent can take a few minutes to start when the instance is busy. If nothing arrives after 10 minutes, start the agent by hand: **AI Agent Studio** > **Agentic Solutions** > **AI agents** tab > agent **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** > **Run test**, test scenario **Review expense event EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01** > **Run single test**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_now_assist_badge_notification.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. This will open the **Now Assist** chat. Click on the two-headed diagonal arrow to Enter **Modal**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_now_assist_chat_expand.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Here is an overview of the steps that were executed.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Extract Cost Center** returns the **cost center** and **vendor** of the expense event.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Search for Cost Center History** returns the cost center's monthly budget and actual spend, and the agent says whether the months are mostly On Target, Over Budget or Under Budget.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Search for Expense Transactions History** returns earlier transactions with the same vendor.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> Finally, **Budget Variance Analysis** returns the cost center's new total spend and, because CC_IT_001 is now over budget, the **Finance Case** it created for further review and action.\n\n#### Completion: Verify Finance Case\n\nNavigate to Finance Operations Workspace. Find the case created by the agent. Confirm it contains the cost center, vendor, and budget analysis.\n\n1. Navigate to Workspaces > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Finance Operations Workspace** and click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> workspace with the same name. We will now check if Finance Case has been created successfully.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_fow_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. For this exercise, we are not impersonating a persona so you remain as the System user.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_fow_system_user.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **list (list icon)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Lists** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> sort by **Number** descending/ascending > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> or look for the Finance case created by the AI agent, with the short description **CC_IT_001 is exceeding budget**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_finance_case_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### Conclusion\n\nCongratulations! With four prompts you have built the **Workflow Data Fabric** integration and the **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** agent that create cases proactively from multiple data sources, so budgets are managed with zero human intervention. The AI Agent is triggered as soon as a new expense event lands in the **Expense Transaction Event** table.\n\n### Next step\n\nLet us continue building the data foundations for AI Agents to use. The next suggested exercise is to go deep dive in the data integrations used by the same agent in this exercise - Zero Copy.\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n",
    "/exercises/zero-copy-connectors": "---\nicon: arrows-to-circle\n---\n\n# Lab Exercise: Zero Copy Connectors\n\n## Where we are in this workshop\n\n<figure><picture><source srcset=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_zero_copy_dark.png\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_zero_copy.png\" alt=\"Zero Copy Connectors focus: Cost Center and Expense data from CDW and ERP\"></picture><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n> **Legend:** 🟤 Data | 🟣 Workflow Data Fabric | 🔵 External Systems | ↓ Takes data from\n\n## Lab Exercise: Zero Copy Connectors\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n\nThis lab will walk you through integration of data coming from Cloud Data Warehouses and ERP using Zero Copy Connectors (ZCC) for SQL and ERP respectively.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_zerocopy_overview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_zerocopy_how_it_works.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_zerocopy_demo_preview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### Lab Sections and Objectives\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#data-flow\">1</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Context Setting:</strong> Review the data flow diagram showing how ServiceNow consumes data from Cloud Data Warehouses and ERP systems via Zero Copy Connectors for SQL and ERP.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**Preparation**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#preparation-platform-configuration\">2</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Platform Configuration:</strong> Complete Integration Hub platform configuration if not done. Assign <code>sn_erp_integration.erp_admin</code> role to admin user.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**Zero Copy Connector for ERP**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#walkthrough-explore-zcc-for-erp-workspace\">3</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>ZCC for ERP Workspace:</strong> Navigate to Zero Copy Connector for ERP Home. Explore the workspace layout.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#hands-on-clone-erp-data-product-for-cost-center\">4</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Clone ERP Data Product:</strong> Clone the OOTB CP: Cost Center model. Label it SAP Cost Center. Assign ERP system S4D.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#walkthrough-explore-zcc-for-erp-bapi-entity\">5</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>ERP BAPI Entity:</strong> Review the BAPI_COSTCENTER_GETDETAIL1 entity. Explore Specify Inputs and Choose Outputs configurations.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#walkthrough-explore-zcc-for-erp-extraction-tables\">6</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>ERP Extraction Tables:</strong> Filter and review SAP Cost Center extraction table. Navigate to the target table containing Cost Center Master Data from SAP.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**Zero Copy Connector for SQL**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#reference-cloud-data-warehouse-source\">7</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Cloud Data Warehouse Source:</strong> Review the PostgreSQL table used as the source for Zero Copy for SQL (the facilitator manages the database).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#walkthrough-navigation-and-review-of-zcc-connection\">8</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>ZCC Connection Review:</strong> Navigate to Zero Copy Connectors. Review the established PostgreSQL connection details.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#hands-on-configure-column-mappings\">9</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Configure Column Mappings:</strong> Create a data fabric table from the PostgreSQL table lab_cc_summary. Set Cost Center as a Reference field to the ERP extraction table. Set GL Account as primary key.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#walkthrough-open-data-fabric-table\">10</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Open Data Fabric Table:</strong> Open the data fabric table and see the rows read live from PostgreSQL.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**AI Agent and Finance Operations Workspace**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#hands-on-test-the-forecast-variance-ai-agent\">11</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Test AI Agent:</strong> Start the Forecast Variance agent (with your initials) you built in Integration Hub from AI Agent Studio. Follow its steps in the trace log, through to the Finance Case.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#completion-verify-finance-case\">12</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Verify the Finance Case:</strong> Navigate to Finance Operations Workspace. Find the case created by the agent.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-zero-copy-connectors.md#conclusion\">13</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Walk through the complete data flow chain showing how Zero Copy Connectors bring external data into ServiceNow for AI Agent-driven case management.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n### Data flow\n\nThe data flow below shows how ServiceNow consumes data from the local Expense Transaction Event table populated by REST API events. The events processed can be near-real-time or historical (e.g. transaction events after over a period of time). Aside from local tables, ServiceNow will also consume external data from a Cloud Data Warehouse and an ERP system via ZCC for SQL and ERP respectively. The data taken from the external sources will be used by an agent which will also create Finance Cases for Cost Centers which are going over budget. While majority of the workflow is handled deterministically, AI Agents will provide additional context by searching and comparing expenses and cost center histories to enrich the workflow data that will be used by the personnel in charge of the cost centers.\n\n**Note**: future versions of this lab will include ServiceNow Enterprise Graph which will provide a universal query functionality that brings together the various internal and external data sources. As of Jan-2026, said feature is not globally available and is hence not yet included in this lab.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"User Interaction Layer\"\n        Employee((Employee/<br/>Finance Manager))\n        EC[Employee Center or<br/> Workspace with Now Assist]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"External Systems\"\n        ERP[(ERP System<br/>OData Endpoint)]\n        CDW[(Cloud Data<br/>Warehouse)]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"ServiceNow AI Platform\"\n        subgraph \"Data Integration Layer\"\n            ZeroCopySQL[Zero Copy SQL<br/>Connection]\n            ZeroCopyERP[Zero Copy ERP<br/>Connection]\n        end\n\n        subgraph \"Zero Copy Tables - Read Only\"\n            ZCCC[(Cost Centre)]\n            ZCCH[(Cost Centre</br>History)]\n            ZCExp[(Expenses)]\n        end\n\n        subgraph \"ServiceNow Native Tables\"\n            ExpenseTable[(Expense Event<br/>Line Items<br/>Scoped Table)]\n            FinCase[(Finance Case<br/>Table)]\n        end\n\n        subgraph \"AI & Automation\"\n            Agent1[Agent: Forecast<br/>Variance]\n            Lookups[Record Lookups]\n\n            FlowAction[Subflows]\n        end\n    end\n\n    %% Data Flow Connections\n    ERP -->|OData Feed| ZeroCopyERP\n    CDW -->|Data Fabric table| ZeroCopySQL\n    ZeroCopyERP --> ZCCC\n    ZeroCopySQL --> ZCCH\n    ZeroCopySQL --> ZCExp\n\n    %% Agent 1 Workflow - Zero Copy Source\n    ZCCC -->|Query Over-Budget| Agent1\n    ZCCH -->|Historical Data| Agent1\n    ZCExp -->|Expense Details| Agent1\n    ExpenseTable -->|Search Similar Cases| Agent1\n    FlowAction -->|Create Case| FinCase\n    Agent1 <-->|Cost Center and<br/>Vendor History| Lookups\n    Agent1 <-->|Extract Cost Center,<br/>Budget Variance Analysis| FlowAction\n\n    %% User Interaction Connections\n    Employee -->|Ask Questions<br/>View/Update Cases| EC\n    EC -->|Search & Query| FinCase\n\n    %% Styling\n    classDef external fill:#2196F3,stroke:#1565C0,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n    classDef user fill:#F5F5F5,stroke:#616161,stroke-width:3px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef nowassist fill:#FFB300,stroke:#F57F17,stroke-width:2px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef platform fill:#4CAF50,stroke:#2E7D32,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n    classDef wdf fill:#9C27B0,stroke:#6A1B9A,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n\n    class ERP,CDW external\n    class ZeroCopySQL,ZeroCopyERP wdf\n    class ZCCC,ZCCH,ZCExp wdf\n    class ExpenseTable,FinCase platform\n    class Agent1,Lookups nowassist\n    class FlowAction platform\n    class Employee,EC user\n```\n\n> **Color Legend:** 🟡 Now Assist | 🟢 Platform | 🟣 Workflow Data Fabric | 🔵 External Systems | ⚪ User Interaction\n>\n> [📊 View High-Resolution Diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/dataflow_zero_copy_connectors.png)\n\nIn this version of the lab, the agent you built in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](lab-exercise-integration-hub.md) reads the cost center budget from the local Cost Center Budget History table. The zero copy tables you set up here show where that data lives in the source systems; pointing the agent at them is a planned extension.\n\n### Preparation\n\n#### Preparation: Platform Configuration\n\nComplete Integration Hub platform configuration if not done. Assign `sn_erp_integration.erp_admin` role to admin user.\n\n1. If you have not done [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-integration-hub) yet, do the needed [Preparation: Platform Configuration](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-integration-hub#preparation-platform-configuration) steps.\n2. Make sure you are logged in as **admin** user.\n3.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Users and Groups** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Users and Groups > Users**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_agent_studio_users_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  Search for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **System Administrator** then hit **Return/Enter ↵** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **admin**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_search_admin_user.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  In the **Roles** tab, click **Edit**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_roles_tab_edit.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n6.  Search for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **sn\\_erp\\_integration.erp\\_admin** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **sn\\_erp\\_integration.erp\\_admin** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click on **>** to move the role to the right panel > then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Save**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_roles_erp_admin_save.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n7.  You will get <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> messages such as **Adding Role decision\\_table\\_reader to admin**, there will be 4 of such messages > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> right-click on the top panel and click **Save**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_role_messages_save.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n8.  <mark style=\"color:red;\">**IMPORTANT**</mark>. Log out and log back in.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_logout.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"254\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### Zero Copy Connector for ERP\n\n#### Walkthrough: Explore ZCC for ERP Workspace\n\nThis provides the steps needed to connect ServiceNow to the ERP system to obtain Cost Center Master data.\n\n1.  Navigate to All > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Zero Copy Connector for ERP Home** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Zero Copy Connector for ERP Home**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_erp_home_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  The **Zero Copy Connector for ERP Home** is a workspace which has the layout as below.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_erp_home_layout.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: Clone ERP Data Product for Cost Center\n\nClone the OOTB CP: Cost Center model. Label it SAP Cost Center. Assign ERP system S4D.\n\n1.  Click on <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Models (database icon)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Model Name** > **more (vertical three dots)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> type **CP: Cost Center** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Apply**. We will replicate the structure of this OOTB data model.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_models_filter_cost_center.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Click on **CP: Cost Center** with Short Description **Data Product: Cost Center ( Function Call )**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_dp_cost_center_click.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Note the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> popup that indicates that you are opening an **ERP Data Product** which is delivered as OOTB templates that customers can use to ramp-up creation of ERP models, which means it cannot be edited. Click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Clone** to create a copy of this model. If one or two guided-tour dialogs open on the model page, close them and answer **No** to **Stop Guided Tour**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_clone_popup.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  Provide the label for the cloned model as <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **SAP Cost Center Lab** and take note of the Target application which should be <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Forecast Variance**. Click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> Clone this model once done.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_clone_model_details.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"450\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  After cloning the model you will be directed to its configuration screen. Assign the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> ERP system name as S4D then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click Save. This will set up your model to use an ERP system that the ServiceNow instance is integrated to via Connections & Credentials. Then, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click **Manage model**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_model_config_save.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on (Build Agent option): Clone ERP Data Product for Cost Center\n\nYou can let Build Agent clone the model for you.\n\n> **Using Build Agent:** go to ServiceNow Studio, open the **Forecast Variance** app, click **Build Agent** (diamond icon) > **New conversation**, then paste the prompt. Build Agent shows each script before running it; click **Approve**. If it asks you a question, answer it in the chat. If you see a 401 error, reload the page and send the prompt again.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_ba_new_conversation.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n1.  Paste this prompt and send it.\n\n    ```\n    Clone the ERP model \"CP: Cost Center\" (Function Call variant) as \"SAP Cost Center Lab\"\n    in the Forecast Variance app, and set its ERP system to S4D.\n    First confirm the system property sn_erp_integration.enableModelModification is true.\n    Method: from a script in the x_snc_forecast_v_0 scope, run the operation_script of the\n    sys_ws_operation \"CloneModel\" in scope sn_erp_integration through GlideScopedEvaluator,\n    with request = { pathParams: { sysId: <source sys_id>, name: <new name> } } and\n    response = {}. Then look up the new model by name and set system. Stop if the name\n    already exists.\n    Report with gs.info: the new model's scope, origin and system, and its counts of\n    operations, entities, table fields, inputs, input mappings and outputs next to the\n    source's. If anything only partially inserts, roll back the run instead of leaving\n    orphans.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve**. You should see the new model in **Forecast Variance** with system **S4D**, and counts that match the source (3, 29, 327, 48, 48, 29).\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_ba_approve.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Walkthrough: Explore ZCC for ERP BAPI Entity\n\nReview the BAPI\\_COSTCENTER\\_GETDETAIL1 entity. Explore Specify Inputs and Choose Outputs configurations.\n\n1.  Click **Read** to use a read-only operation configured in the model. ZCC for ERP models can also perform **Update** and **Create** actions.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_click_read.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  There is a BAPI already included in the **CP: Cost Center** model you have cloned earlier. The entity **BAPI\\_COSTCENTER\\_GETDETAIL1** is already configured here so you do not have to do anything. As mentioned earlier, there are other ways to obtain master data from SAP (whether it is Cost Center, Materials, etc.) such as RFC table reads or OData endpoints.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_bapi_configured.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Click on **Specify Inputs**. You do not need to do anything in this screen. The intent is to provide an overview of what can be configured as fields for selections when extracting or displaying information from the ERP system. If the table, BAPI, or OData endpoint supports it, this screen can also be left blank which is an equivalent of selecting all rows/records when executing the **Read** action.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_specify_inputs.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  Click on **Choose outputs**. You do not need to do anything in this screen. The intent is to provide an overview of what can be configured as the output for your selection or extraction. Both **Specify inputs** and **Choose outputs** sections can be intimidating for non-SAP practitioners which led to the creation of the **Data Product** we cloned in **Step 5**. Find out more about [**ERP Data Products here**](https://store.servicenow.com/store/app/9a0ad9f41b19e650396216db234bcba9).\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_choose_outputs.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Walkthrough: Explore ZCC for ERP Extraction Tables\n\nFilter and review SAP Cost Center extraction table. Navigate to the target table containing Cost Center Master Data from SAP.\n\n1.  Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Extraction tables (Sankey diagram icon)** and click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Name** > **more (vertical three dots)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> type **SAP Cost Center** and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Apply**. **Extraction tables** are used as persistence layer for **ERP models**, i.e. data is stored here from Extract Transform Load (ETL) processes as an alternative to reading ERP data via Zero Copy. This is useful especially if the ERP table you are connecting to has millions of rows OR are not frequently updated. In our use case, while cost center master data is relatively small in many customer environments, they do not change frequently.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_extraction_tables_filter.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Click on **SAP Cost Center**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_sap_cost_center_click.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  There is a notification stating that <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> the object is in the **Zero Copy Connector for ERP application**, this is expected. Note that the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **ERP model** used here is different from what you have created earlier, this uses **SAP Material Transfer Cost Center**, this configuration is expected. This discrepancy is because we are not connected to a live SAP system for this exercise. The tools and configurations you have used are representative of a real SAP integration. Finally, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click on the **Target table link** which is **sn\\_erp\\_integration\\_cost\\_center\\_list.do**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_target_table_link.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4. This will lead to the extraction table which contains **Cost Center Master Data** from SAP. This exercise uses an extraction scenario where data from SAP is stored in ServiceNow.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_cc_target_table_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5. Congratulations! You have set-up the integration to a Cloud Data Warehouse using Zero Copy Connector for ERP.\n\n#### Additional Reading: Direct online read for ZCC for ERP\n\n1. Direct online read is also possible with more details found on the blog post [Zero Copy Connector for ERP guide by Leo Francia in the ServiceNow community](https://www.servicenow.com/community/app-engine-for-erp-blogs/part-1-of-4-intelligent-erp-workflows-get-sap-data-into/ba-p/3192800).\n\n### Zero Copy Connector for SQL\n\n#### Reference: Cloud Data Warehouse Source\n\nIn this lab the cloud data warehouse is a **PostgreSQL** database hosted on Neon. Its table **lab\\_cc\\_summary** holds the 2025 actual and baseline spend for 24 cost centers, one row per cost center and GL account: cost\\_center, gl\\_account, fiscal\\_year, period, actual\\_amount\\_usd, baseline\\_amount\\_usd, variance, variance\\_pct, forecast\\_source and last\\_updated. Your facilitator has connected it to the instance with a read-only login, so no action needs to be done for this step.\n\n#### Walkthrough: Navigation and Review of ZCC Connection\n\nNavigate to Zero Copy Connectors. Review the established PostgreSQL connection.\n\n1.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Zero Copy Connectors** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Zero Copy Connectors (Workflow Data Fabric)**. This opens the **Zero Copy Connector Hub**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_nav.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"320\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Go to **Established connections** > **Forecast Variance Postgres**. <mark style=\"color:red;\">**Note:**</mark> this connection is configured specifically for instances used in ServiceNow-led labs. <mark style=\"color:red;\">**lab.service-now.com instances:**</mark> the connection is not there. The hub lists only **Apache Iceberg**, **SAP ECC** and **SAP S/4HANA** under **Available connectors**, and the **Established connections** are Alectri Finance FV, AlectriBigQuery, AlectriOracle, AlectriRedshift, ServiceNow local instance and Snowflake Connection. There is no **Forecast Variance Postgres** connection and no PostgreSQL tile, so the PostgreSQL parts of this page cannot be done until your facilitator adds the connection.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_established.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"560\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  The **Connection details** tab shows how the connection is configured: <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> a JDBC URL to the Neon database and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> the read-only user **wdf\\_lab\\_reader**. No action needs to be done for this step.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_connection_details.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"560\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: Configure Column Mappings\n\nCreate a data fabric table from lab\\_cc\\_summary. Set Cost Center as a Reference field to the ERP extraction table. Set GL Account as primary key.\n\n1.  Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Data assets** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **public**, and beside **lab\\_cc\\_summary** <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click **Create data fabric table**. This screen lists the tables in the database; this lab uses only **lab\\_cc\\_summary**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_data_assets.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Enter the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Label**, e.g. **cc\\_summ\\_\\<your initials>**. The <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Name** is filled in for you, e.g. **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_df\\_cc\\_summ\\_lfr**, and must stay at 40 characters or fewer. Check that <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Application scope** shows **Forecast Variance**, then click **Continue**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_df_label.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"560\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Tick the box beside **Name** to map all 10 columns to the data fabric table. You can also pick only the columns you need, which makes the table load faster.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_select_columns.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  For **cost\\_center**, change <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Type** from **String** to **Reference** (at the end of the list), then click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Set Reference**. A **Reference** field points to a record in another table, so each cost center links to its master data from SAP.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_cost_center_reference.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  Set <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Table** to **SAP Cost Center** (**sn\\_erp\\_integration\\_cost\\_center**, which you set up in the ZCC for ERP exercise) and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Reference key** to **Cost Center**, then click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Set Reference**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_set_reference.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"444\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n6.  Turn on <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Primary** for **gl\\_account**, then click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Finish**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_primary_key.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n7.  In the **Primary key defined** dialog, click **Confirm**. A primary key lets ServiceNow tell the source rows apart, and it can't be removed later.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_confirm_pk.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Walkthrough: Open Data Fabric Table\n\nView the data fabric table you created and open its contents.\n\n1.  Your table now shows under **lab\\_cc\\_summary**. Click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> the three vertical dots > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Open list**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_open_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  The list shows all 24 rows, read from PostgreSQL when you open it. The data stays in the source database; nothing is copied into ServiceNow.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_zcc_pg_df_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Congratulations! You have set up the integration to a Cloud Data Warehouse using Zero Copy Connector for SQL.\n\n#### Hands-on (Build Agent option): Give the Agent the PostgreSQL Data\n\nBuild Agent adds a tool to the **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** agent that reads your data fabric table, so the agent can compare the cost center's PostgreSQL summary with its budget history.\n\n1.  In a new conversation, paste this prompt, replace **\\<your table name>** with the name of your table from the previous exercise (for example **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_df\\_cc\\_summ\\_lfr**), replace **\\<your initials>** with your initials (for example **LF**) and send it.\n\n    ```\n    In the Forecast Variance app, add a tool to the existing AI agent\n    \"Forecast Variance <your initials>\",\n    named \"Search for Cost Center Summary\", that runs without asking. It looks up up to 12\n    records in the table <your table name> by cost center, ordered by period, and returns\n    period, fiscal year, actual amount, baseline amount, variance and variance percent. In\n    the agent instructions, add this step after Step 3 and renumber the later steps: \"Step\n    4: Review PostgreSQL Cost Center Summary. Use the Search for Cost Center Summary tool\n    with the cost center from Step 1 and say whether the variance is mostly positive or\n    negative.\" Keep the agent's other tools, instructions and trigger as they are, and keep\n    the trigger on. Build and install the app without creating test records.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve** each time Build Agent asks. You should see the new **Search for Cost Center Summary** tool and a **Step 4: Review PostgreSQL Cost Center Summary** in the agent's instructions, with the earlier tools and the trigger still in place.\n\n### AI Agent and Finance Operations Workspace\n\n#### Hands-on: Test the Forecast Variance AI Agent\n\nThe **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** agent you built in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](lab-exercise-integration-hub.md) checks each new expense event. Here you start it by hand from AI Agent Studio, so you can follow each step in the trace log.\n\n**Before you test:** the test processes the event **EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01**, so that record has to exist. [Open the Expense Transaction Event list](/x_snc_forecast_v_0_expense_transaction_event_list.do) and look for it. If the list shows **No records to display**, create the event again with step 4 of **Hands-on: Flow Execution** in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](lab-exercise-integration-hub.md), then continue with the steps below. Without the event the agent reports the review as complete but the **Cost center extracted** step fails.\n\n1.  Navigate to All > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **AI Agent Studio** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Agentic Solutions**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_agentic_solutions_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Select the **AI agents** tab, type **Forecast Variance** in **Search** and click your agent **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>**. The agent opens as a canvas. Click **Run test**.\n3.  In the **Run a test** dialog, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> keep **Single test** selected, under <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Test scenario** pick **Review expense event EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01** (or type it under **or write your own**) and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click **Run single test**. The event has to exist first; see **Hands-on: Flow Execution** in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](lab-exercise-integration-hub.md).\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_run_test_dialog.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  The **Trace log** opens on the right and shows each tool as it runs: **Extract Cost Center**, **Search for Cost Center History**, **Search for Expense Transactions History**, **Search for Cost Center Summary** (if you added it) and **Budget Variance Analysis**. Budget Variance Analysis can take a few minutes when the instance is busy. Wait until the test shows **Completed**.\n5.  When the test ends, the answer shows the cost center and vendor, the cost center's monthly budget history, the vendor's earlier transactions, and the **Finance Case** that Budget Variance Analysis created because CC_IT_001 is over budget.\n\n#### Completion: Verify Finance Case\n\nNavigate to Finance Operations Workspace. Find the case created by the agent.\n\n1. Navigate to Workspaces > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Finance Operations Workspace** and click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> workspace with the same name.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_fow_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. For this exercise, we are not impersonating a persona so you remain as the System user.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_fow_system_user.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **list (list icon)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Lists** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> sort by **Number** descending/ascending > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> or look for the Finance case created by the AI Agent, with the short description **CC_IT_001 is exceeding budget**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_finance_case_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### Conclusion\n\nCongratulations! You have created the **Workflow Data Fabric** integrations that powers the **Financial Forecast Variance Agent** allowing proactive creation of cases based on multiple data sources in a complex landscape to allow proactive management of budgets.\n\n### Next step\n\nLet us continue building the data foundations for AI Agents to use. The next suggested exercise is the creation of the External Content Connector to SharePoint.\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n",
    "/exercises/lens-and-document-intelligence": "---\nicon: file-magnifying-glass\n---\n\n# Lab Exercise: ServiceNow Document Intelligence and Lens\n\n## Where we are in this workshop\n\n<figure><picture><source srcset=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_doc_intelligence_dark.png\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_doc_intelligence.png\" alt=\"Document Intelligence focus: Expense to Documents\"></picture><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n> **Legend:** 🟤 Data | 🟡 Now Assist | 🔵 External Systems | ↓ Takes data from\n\n## Lab Exercise: ServiceNow Document Intelligence and Lens\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n\nThis lab will walk you through the configuration and usage of ServiceNow Lens and Document Intelligence as sources of unstructured document data for interactive and batch capture of expense information from documents.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_lens_docintel_overview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_docintel_demo_preview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n**A note on this exercise:** In production, invoices are captured at the source: an ERP, procurement platform, or expense system, not uploaded directly into ServiceNow. ServiceNow's strength in this pattern is what happens _after_ ingestion: orchestrating validation against external data, enriching records via integration, and routing exceptions through case management. That's the capability we're demonstrating in most of the exercises in this lab.\n\nTo keep this exercise self-contained and reuse the agent built in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-integration-hub), we upload the document to a task record and let Document Intelligence extract it locally. Once the document is extracted, everything downstream such as the agent calls, the cross-system lookups, and the case creation, works the same regardless of how the document arrived. The document upload through a task table is a stand-in for the real action that happens in an ERP system. This exercise is about what ServiceNow _does_ with the document and is not about how it _receives_ it.\n\nA more detailed version of this exercise with significantly more configuration steps is available as standalone. Reach out to your Lab Administrator for more details.\n\n### Lab Sections and Objectives\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#data-flow\">1</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Context Setting:</strong> Review the data flow diagram showing how ServiceNow captures information from documents via Lens and Document Intelligence.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**Document Intelligence**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#walkthrough-document-intelligence-setup\">2</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Document Intelligence Setup:</strong> Navigate to AI Admin Hub > AI Skills. Activate the Extract information from documents skill. Review the Expense Transaction Event use case configuration and integrations.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#hands-on-document-intelligence-parameters\">3</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Document Intelligence Parameters:</strong> Set extraction thresholds to 0.01 in Global scope for lab purposes.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#hands-on-document-intelligence-runtime\">4</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Document Intelligence Runtime:</strong> Create a variance task record. Upload the Invoice_IT_Laptop_CC_IT_002.pdf document. Set state to Work in Progress and submit.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#walkthrough-forecast-variance-ai-agent\">5</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Watch the AI Agent React:</strong> Look for the Now Assist badge. Open Now Assist chat. Expand to Modal view. Review the cost center and vendor, the budget and vendor history, and the Finance Case link.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#completion-verify-finance-case\">6</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Verify the Finance Case:</strong> Navigate to Finance Operations Workspace. Find the case created by the agent.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#optional-completion-verify-document-output\">7</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>[Optional] Verify Document Output:</strong> Navigate to AI Admin Hub > AI Skills. Review the extracted document information in the Test Outputs tab.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**AI Lens**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#walkthrough-ai-lens-setup\">8</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>AI Lens Setup:</strong> Navigate to AI Admin Hub > AI Skills. Activate ServiceNow AI Lens.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#walkthrough-ai-lens-download\">9</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>AI Lens Download:</strong> Download and install the Lens application for your device.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#hands-on-ai-lens-runtime\">10</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>AI Lens Runtime:</strong> Open the Invoice_Injection_PROD_DE_2.pdf document. Navigate to the Expense Transaction Event table. Use Create with Lens to capture and submit expense data.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-servicenow-lens-and-document-intelligence.md#conclusion\">11</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Walk through the capabilities of both Document Intelligence and AI Lens for document-based data capture.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n### Data flow\n\nThe data flow below shows how ServiceNow will get information from documents from invoices and further process said information to evaluate whether a Finance case should be created.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"User Interaction Layer\"\n        Employee((Employee/<br/>Finance Manager))\n        EC[Employee Center or<br/>Workspace with Now Assist]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"ServiceNow AI Platform\"\n        subgraph \"ServiceNow Native Tables\"\n            ExpenseTable[(Expense Event<br/>Line Items<br/>Scoped Table)]\n            BudgetTable[(Cost Center<br/>Budget History<br/>Scoped Table)]\n            FinCase[(Finance Case<br/>Table)]\n        end\n\n        subgraph \"AI & Automation\"\n            Agent1[Agent: Forecast<br/>Variance]\n            Lookups[Record Lookups]\n            FlowAction[Subflows]\n        end\n        subgraph \"AI Experiences\"\n            Lens[\"ServiceNow</br>Lens\"]\n            DocIntel[\"Document</br>Intelligence\"]\n        end\n    end\n\n\n    %% Data Flow Connections\n    EC -->|Individual UI-based| Lens -->|Write| ExpenseTable\n    EC -->|Individual UI-based| DocIntel -->|Write| ExpenseTable\n\n    %% Agent Workflow\n    ExpenseTable -->|Incoming Event| Agent1\n    BudgetTable -->|Current Budget| Agent1\n    Agent1 <-->|Cost Center and<br/>Vendor History| Lookups\n    Agent1 <-->|Extract Cost Center,<br/>Budget Variance Analysis| FlowAction\n    FlowAction -->|Create Case| FinCase\n\n    %% User Interaction Connections\n    Employee -->|Ask Questions<br/>View/Update Cases| EC\n    EC -->|Search & Query| FinCase\n\n\n    %% Styling\n    classDef user fill:#F5F5F5,stroke:#616161,stroke-width:3px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef nowassist fill:#FFB300,stroke:#F57F17,stroke-width:2px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef platform fill:#4CAF50,stroke:#2E7D32,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n\n    class ExpenseTable,BudgetTable,FinCase platform\n    class Agent1,Lookups nowassist\n    class FlowAction platform\n    class Lens,DocIntel nowassist\n    class Employee,EC user\n```\n\n> **Color Legend:** 🟡 Now Assist | 🟢 Platform | 🟣 Workflow Data Fabric | 🔵 External Systems | ⚪ User Interaction\n>\n> [📊 View High-Resolution Diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/dataflow_lens_document_intelligence.png)\n\n### Document Intelligence\n\n#### Walkthrough: Document Intelligence Setup\n\nNavigate to AI Admin Hub > AI Skills. Activate the Extract information from documents skill. Review the Expense Transaction Event use case configuration and integrations.\n\n1.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **AI Admin Hub** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **AI Admin Hub > AI Skills** (the page can take up to a minute to load).\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_now_assist_skills_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Platform** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Other** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> type **Extract information from documents** > go to **Extract information from documents** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark>**&#x20;Edit Configuration** (a button on the skill card).\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_edit_extract_skill.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Create Usecase** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Expense Transaction Event.**\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_create_usecase.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4. In this screen, you do not have to configure anything as this has been preconfigured as a custom **use case** under the standard platform skill **Extract information from documents**. The sub-steps below only serve as a tour of the different configuration components for a Document Intelligence components.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark>**&#x20;Status: Active** indicates that this has been activated prior.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Target table: Expense Transaction Event** is the table that will save the extracted information from the documents. This can be a standard or a custom table\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark>**&#x20;Full automation mode: On** indicates that this skill will automatically process and extract the information from uploaded documents. If [Document Intelligence Admin](https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/8700f4efc3a411101d9a3cadb140ddad/1.1.0) is installed, the thresholds fore **Full automation** to trigger can be set for each use case. Our scenario does not have it installed so we will configure the thresholds for Full automation mode in the latter steps.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark>**&#x20;Field Names** show all of the relevant fields for this use case, these have been preconfigured.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**e.)**</mark>**&#x20;Target fields** show the fields from the **Target table** where the extracted information will be saved in.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**f.)**</mark>**&#x20;Type** is where the data type can be configured. For this scenario we are using Text for all as Document Intelligence is capable of mapping this to the appropriate data type in the target table in most cases.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**g.)**</mark> **Required** can be configured to set whether a field is mandatory for the Document Intelligence extraction, i.e. a blank required field will result into the extraction not being saved into the target table.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**h.)**</mark>**&#x20;+ New field** allows addition of new fields for Document Intelligence to extract. No additional fields are needed for this scenario.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**i.)**</mark>**&#x20;Settings (gear icon)** allow you to toggle **Full Automation mode** and **Manage LLMs**.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**j.)**</mark> Go to **Integrations** tab.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_usecase_config_overview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5. In the integrations tab the following needs to be observed. The **Process** integration picks up the document from the source table and **Extract** integration extracts the contents of the document to be saved to the target table.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark>**&#x20;Extract** integration should be present with the target table **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_expense\\_transaction\\_event (Expense Transaction Event)**.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;DocIntel Extract Values Flow - Expense Transaction Event - Extract** should be the Flow assigned. If it is not assigned, double click and type the name of the flow to assign it. This is a scoped Flow and is created specifically for this use case.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark>**&#x20;Process** integration should be present with the target table **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_expense\\_transaction\\_event (Expense Transaction Event)**.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark>**&#x20;DocIntel Task Processing Flow - Expense Transaction Event - Process** should be the Flow assigned. If it is not assigned, double click and type the name of the flow to assign it. This is a scoped Flow and is created specifically for this use case.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**e.)**</mark> If everything is correct, click **Exit**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_integrations_tab.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n6. Click **Save and Continue**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_save_and_continue.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n7.  Click **Activate**. <mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**Note:**</mark> If the skill is already activated, just click **Done**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_activate.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n8.  Click **Return to Platform**. <mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**Note:**</mark> If the skill is already activated, this modal pop-up will not appear.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_return_to_platform.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"563\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n9.  You will be redirected to the Skills screen and this concludes the walkthrough of the Skills needed for document extraction.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_skills_screen.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: Document Intelligence Parameters\n\n1. Steps 2 to 4 are applicable if you do **NOT** have [Document Intelligence Admin](https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/8700f4efc3a411101d9a3cadb140ddad/1.1.0) plugin installed which is the case for this lab. Succeeding versions of this lab will have the said plugin installed which will result in a more streamlined experience.\n2.  For this step, change the scope to Global by navigating to the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **globe icon** and clicking <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Global** application scope. (On the property form you can also click the banner link **To edit this record click here**, which does the same.)\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_scope_global.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"321\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3. Navigate to All > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Document Data Extraction** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click Document **Data Extraction > System Properties**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_doc_extraction_nav.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"373\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. Search for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **\\*threshold** and update the values of the three parameters below <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> to **0.01**. This is to reduce the threshold for the automation and avoid trial and error issues. In a production environment, you are likely to test and fine-tune this to ensure exceptions are caught and corrected manually.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_threshold_search.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5. Change the scope back by navigating to the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **globe icon** and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> searching and/or clicking **Forecast Variance** application scope.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_scope_forecast_variance.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"319\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on (Build Agent option): Document Intelligence Parameters\n\nYou can let Build Agent set the three properties for you, without switching scope.\n\n> **Using Build Agent:** go to ServiceNow Studio, open the **Forecast Variance** app, click **Build Agent** (diamond icon) > **New conversation**, then paste the prompt. Build Agent shows each script before running it; click **Approve**. If it asks you a question, answer it in the chat. If you see a 401 error, reload the page and send the prompt again.\n\n1.  Paste this prompt and send it.\n\n    ```\n    In global scope, set these three system properties to 0.01 and report their old and new\n    values with gs.info:\n    glide.platform_ml_di.doc_data_extractor.warning_score_threshold,\n    glide.platform_ml_di.doc_data_extractor.autofill_threshold,\n    glide.platform_ml_di.doc_data_extractor.straight_through_processing_threshold.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve**. You should see all three properties at **0.01**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_ldi_ba_props.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: Document Intelligence Runtime\n\nCreate a variance task record. Upload the Invoice\\_IT\\_Laptop\\_CC\\_IT\\_002.pdf document. Set state to Work in Progress and submit.\n\n1.  Go to **All** > type **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_variance\\_task.do** and hit **Return/Enter ↵**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_variance_task_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2. We will be uploading a document in the **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_variance\\_task** task table. As mentioned earlier in this lab, ServiceNow is not a usual source of uploaded invoices as invoice uploads are normally done in ERP systems. The objective of these next steps is to show how ServiceNow would be able to capture information from similar documents and process them upstream. **Remember the automatically generated task ID!** Your task ID might differ from what is displayed in this screen, will need this later. Follow the steps below:\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_upload_document.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> Put **CC\\_IT\\_002** as the short description. You can make it as descriptive as you like, the intent is to identify this as a document upload for this cost center.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> Click the **Attach (**[**paper clip**](https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/ai-and-paperclip-problem)**)** button.\n\n2. Obtain the invoice file to attach which is a sample invoice for CC\\_IT\\_002 cost center. File here: [**Invoice\\_IT\\_Laptop\\_CC\\_IT\\_002.pdf**](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeA/refs/heads/main/.gitbook/assets/Invoice_IT_Laptop_CC_IT_002.pdf).\n3.  Click **Choose file**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_choose_file.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  Upload the file > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> [**Invoice\\_IT\\_Laptop\\_CC\\_IT\\_002.pdf**](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeA/refs/heads/main/.gitbook/assets/Invoice_IT_Laptop_CC_IT_002.pdf) > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Exit (x)**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_upload_file_exit.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  Go to field > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark>**&#x20;State** and > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> change it to **Work in Progress**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_state_wip.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n6.  You can _either_ <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> right-click on the header and click **Save** or > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> simply click **Submit**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_save_or_submit.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on (Build Agent option): Document Intelligence Runtime\n\nYou can let Build Agent create the task and attach the invoice for you.\n\n1.  In the same chat, paste this prompt and send it.\n\n    ```\n    In the Forecast Variance app, create a record in x_snc_forecast_v_0_variance_task with short\n    description \"CC_IT_002\". Attach the invoice from\n    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeA/refs/heads/main/.gitbook/assets/Invoice_IT_Laptop_CC_IT_002.pdf\n    to that record with RESTMessageV2.saveResponseBodyAsAttachment before execute(), keeping the\n    file name. Set that attachment's content type to application/pdf (update its\n    sys_attachment record), then set State to Work in Progress and save the record.\n    Report with gs.info the task number, its state, and the attachment's file name and size.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve**. You should see the new task in **Work in Progress** with the invoice attached. Document Intelligence then reads it and the agent takes over.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/sc_ldi_ba_runtime.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"420\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on (Build Agent option, optional): Set the Owner on Expense Events\n\nThis step is optional. The agent's trigger runs as System Administrator, so a blank **Owner** does not stop it. Build Agent adds a rule that fills **Owner** with the user who creates the event, for tidy records.\n\n1.  In a new conversation, paste this prompt and send it.\n\n    ```\n    In the Forecast Variance app, add a business rule named \"Set Expense Event Owner\" on the\n    Expense Transaction Event table. It runs before insert, and when Owner is empty it sets\n    Owner to the user who is creating the record. Keep the agent, its tools and its trigger as\n    they are, and keep the trigger on. Build and install the app without creating test records.\n    ```\n2.  Click **Approve** each time Build Agent asks. You should see the **Set Expense Event Owner** business rule installed ([open the list](/sys_script_list.do?sysparm_query=name=Set%20Expense%20Event%20Owner)), and the agent's trigger still on.\n\n#### Walkthrough: Forecast Variance AI Agent\n\nLook for the Now Assist badge. Open Now Assist chat. Expand to Modal view. Review the cost center and vendor, the budget and vendor history, and the Finance Case link.\n\n1. In the same browser window, you will notice that there is a new **Now Assist badge**. This is the AI agent at work in the back end. Changing the state of the task with the invoice started the Document Intelligence integration flows, which wrote the invoice to the **Expense Transaction Event** table, and the new record started the **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** agent you built in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-integration-hub). Click on the **Otto/sparkle icon** with the updated badge count. <mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**Note:**</mark> If the **Now Assist badge** does not appear, simply reload your page as it may run slow in demo or lab instances or click on the **Otto/sparkle icon** anyway and wait for a new **Active** chat to appear, indicated by a red dot beside it. Extraction and the agent can take a few minutes when the instance is busy. If nothing arrives after 10 minutes, start the agent by hand: **AI Agent Studio** > **Agentic Solutions** > **AI agents** tab > agent **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** > **Run test**, under **or write your own** type **Review expense event EXP-2025-IT-002-1010-01** > **Run single test**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_now_assist_badge_notification.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2.  This will open the **Now Assist** chat. Click on the two-headed diagonal arrow to Enter **Modal**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ihub_now_assist_chat_expand.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3. Here is an overview of the steps the agent ran for the invoice's event **EXP-2025-IT-002-1010-01**: the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> map shows the agent and its tools, and the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> trace log lists each step.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Extract Cost Center** looks up the expense event by its **Event ID** and returns the **cost center** (**CC_IT_002**) and **vendor** (**TechSource Solutions Inc.**) that Document Intelligence read from the invoice. We use **Event ID** so the agent built in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/lab-exercise-integration-hub) works unchanged. In a real business scenario, the relevant field would be the invoice ID or something similar for this document type.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Search for Cost Center History** returns the cost center's monthly budget and actual spend.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Search for Expense Transactions History** looks for earlier transactions with the same vendor. There are none for TechSource Solutions Inc.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> Finally, **Budget Variance Analysis** returns the cost center's new total spend and, because CC_IT_002 is now over budget, the **Finance Case** it created for further review and action.\n\nIf you started the agent by hand, the **Trace log** in **AI Agent Studio** shows the same four tools as they run.\n\n#### Completion: Verify Finance Case\n\nNavigate to Finance Operations Workspace. Find the case created by the agent.\n\n1. Navigate to Workspaces > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **Finance Operations Workspace** and click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> workspace with the same name.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_fow_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. For this exercise, we are not impersonating a persona so you remain as the System user.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_fow_system_user.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **list (list icon)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Lists** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> sort by **Number** descending/ascending > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> or look for the Finance case created by the AI agent, with the short description **CC_IT_002 is exceeding budget**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_finance_case_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. Congratulations! You have walked through the configuration and runtime of Document Intelligence, integrated with AI Agents that process the contents of the invoice for appropriate case handling for over-budget cost centers.\n\n#### \\[Optional] Completion: Verify Document Output\n\nNavigate to AI Admin Hub > AI Skills. Review the extracted document information in the Test Outputs tab.\n\n1. Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **AI Admin Hub** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **AI Admin Hub > AI Skills** (the page can take up to a minute to load).\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_now_assist_skills_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Platform** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Other** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> type **Extract information from documents** > go to **Extract information from documents** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark>**&#x20;Edit Configuration** (a button on the skill card).\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_edit_extract_skill.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Create Usecase** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Expense Transaction Event.**\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_create_usecase.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. In the screen that follows, go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Test Outputs** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> note the **Task ID** automatically generated when you created an entry in **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_variance\\_task**. Your task ID may differ from what is shown here. Finally, > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> > click on **Process**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_test_outputs.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5.  You can do several things here. Notice the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Invoice** you uploaded with the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;information** now extracted. You can also see the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark>**&#x20;Status**. You also have the option to open the section into a new **Document Intelligence** window.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_extracted_info_view.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### AI Lens\n\n**ServiceNow AI Lens** is a capability that allows capturing of information from documents and images via UI (dialog) with the use of AI. Unlike Document Intelligence which can execute in the back-end (e.g. by picking information from documents attached in cases or tasks), Lens requires user interaction. Also unlike Document Intelligence, Lens requires less set-up upfront.\n\n#### Walkthrough: AI Lens Setup\n\nNavigate to AI Admin Hub > AI Skills. Activate ServiceNow AI Lens.\n\n1.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **AI Admin Hub** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **AI Admin Hub > AI Skills** (the page can take up to a minute to load).\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_now_assist_skills_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Go to <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Platform** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Other** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> type **ServiceNow AI Lens** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> click **Turn on**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_turn_on.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Accept defaults and click **Turn on**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_accept_defaults.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  A pop-up will appear, click **Back to skills**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_back_to_skills.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"563\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5. The **Lens** version in used in the lab is 3.01. If you have already obtained Lens for your own use, skip steps 6 and 7.\n\n#### Walkthrough: AI Lens Download\n\nDownload and install the Lens application for your device.\n\n1.  Navigate to **All** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **ServiceNow AI Lens** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **ServiceNow AI Lens > Downloads and Preferences**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_downloads_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Download and install the appropriate Lens installation package for your device. As there are three possible device types, installation steps are not shown in this guide. It is generally safe to follow the default prompts in the installation package. The page also offers a browser version of Lens that needs no installation; set **Default app on launch** to **Browser** if you prefer it. On lab.service-now.com builds **Browser (no installation required)** is already the default: skip the installation, then use **Create with Lens** to open the browser Lens page (**Upload** and **Capture screen**). On the 7021 test run the **Upload** dialog accepted the PDF but the **Analyze** run stayed at **Processing files...** with no result, so the AI Lens check could not be completed there.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_download_packages.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Hands-on: AI Lens Runtime\n\nObtain the invoice file to attach which is a sample invoice for **PROD\\_DE\\_2** cost center. File here: [**Invoice\\_Injection\\_PROD\\_DE\\_2.pdf**](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeA/refs/heads/main/.gitbook/assets/Invoice_Injection_PROD_DE_2.pdf)**.** Open the file once you have downloaded it.\n\n1.  Go to **All** > type **x\\_snc\\_forecast\\_v\\_0\\_expense\\_transaction\\_event.list** and hit **Return/Enter ↵**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_expense_event_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n2.  Click **Create with Lens** which can be found at the top right portion of the navigation.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_create_with_lens.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  This will open a pop-up. <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> Decide whether you want to always allow your instance to open the app associated with the **Create with Lens button**, i.e. ServiceNow Lens. Having this box ticked or unticked will not affect the Lens app's execution. Then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Open ServiceNow AI Lens.app**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_open_app.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  This will open the **Lens** app. <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> Drag the **Lens** app displayed as a frame with green and indigo gradient. You might instinctively drag the app by just clicking at the frame - you don't have to do this! You can also click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> space inside the frame if you wish to drag it. You can also <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> resize the frame to capture the relevant area of the document. Click **Analyze** once you are done and wait for a few seconds for Lens to process the document.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_frame_analyze.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  Your **Expense Transaction Event** new record in your browser will be populated with the data from the invoice. As with any AI solution, processing time is required which makes important to weigh the benefit of a UI-based document scanner against a backend-friendly solution like Document Intelligence. Click **Submit**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_record_populated.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n6.  The new **Expense Transaction Event** is now saved.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_ldi_lens_event_saved.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### Conclusion\n\nCongratulations! You now have explored the capabilities of both Document Intelligence and AI Lens.\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n",
    "/exercises/mcp-server-client": "---\nicon: mcp\n---\n\n# Lab Exercise: Model Context Protocol Server/Client\n\n## Where we are in this workshop\n\n<figure><picture><source srcset=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_mcp_dark.png\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/dataflow_outcome_agent_flow_mcp.png\" alt=\"MCP focus: External DB to External MCP Server\"></picture><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n> **Legend:** 🟤 Data | 🟣 Workflow Data Fabric | 🔵 External Systems | ↓ Takes data from\n\n## Lab Exercise: Model Context Protocol Server/Client\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n\nThis lab will walk you through the configuration and usage of MCP ([Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/getting-started/intro)) capabilities to interact with ServiceNow either as a client or as a server, allowing end users to interact with the platform as they see fit. For simplicity, this lab will cover ServiceNow acting as an MCP Client. More details on MCP Server scenarios will be added soon.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_mcp_overview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_slide_mcp_demo_preview.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\nSpecifically, this provides the steps needed to connect ServiceNow to an MCP Server tool configured in Neon.\n\nThis exercise does not cover the creation of the MCP Service from Neon as that requires administrator rights and CDW expertise which may not be widely available to various personas.\n\n### Lab Sections and Objectives\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-model-context-protocol-server-client.md#data-flow\">1</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Context Setting:</strong> Review the data flow diagram showing how ServiceNow provides MCP client and server capabilities to interact with external systems.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**MCP Client Configuration**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-model-context-protocol-server-client.md#hands-on-configure-mcp-client\">2</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Configure MCP Client:</strong> Navigate to AI Agent Studio Settings. Add a new MCP Server entry for Neon with API Key authentication.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**AI Agent Configuration**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-model-context-protocol-server-client.md#hands-on-configure-new-ai-agent-for-mcp-scenario\">3</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Configure new AI Agent:</strong> Duplicate your Forecast Variance agent (with your initials). Rename it to Forecast Variance Neon MCP Lab.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-model-context-protocol-server-client.md#hands-on-configure-mcp-step-and-tool\">4</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Configure MCP Step and Tool:</strong> Add MCP instructions to the agent specialty. Add the variance-baseline-search MCP server tool from Neon. Configure tool name, description, and execution mode.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-model-context-protocol-server-client.md#walkthrough-complete-ai-agent-configuration\">5</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Complete AI Agent Configuration:</strong> Accept default security controls. Configure channels and status. Save and test.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n**AI Agent Testing**\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-model-context-protocol-server-client.md#hands-on-test-and-review-custom-ai-agent\">6</a></td><td>Student</td><td><strong>Test AI Agent:</strong> Enter test prompt to process an expense event. Verify the MCP tool returns matching cost center data from Neon.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n<table><thead><tr><th width=\"83\">Step</th><th width=\"106\">Who</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"lab-exercise-model-context-protocol-server-client.md#conclusion\">7</a></td><td>Facilitator</td><td><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Walk through how MCP allows ServiceNow to connect to external systems using LLM-powered integrations as an alternative to traditional APIs.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n### Data flow\n\nThe data flow below shows how ServiceNow provides MCP client and server capabilities.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"User Interaction Layer\"\n        Employee((Employee/<br/>Finance Manager))\n        ClaudeDesktop[Claude Desktop<br/>+ MCP]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"External Systems\"\n        CDW[(Cloud Data<br/>Warehouse)]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"ServiceNow AI Platform\"\n        subgraph \"ServiceNow Native Tables\"\n            FinCase[(Finance Case<br/>Table)]\n            FinVar[(Financial Variance<br/>Table)]\n        end\n\n        subgraph AI[AI & Automation]\n            Agent1[Agent: Forecast<br/>Variance Neon<br/>MCP Lab]\n            MCPS[MCP Server]\n            MCPC[MCP Client]\n        end\n    end\n\n    %% MCP Server Connection\n    FinVar -->|Query Data| MCPS\n    FinCase -->|Query Data| MCPS\n    MCPS <-->|API Communication| ClaudeDesktop\n\n    %% MCP Client Connection\n    Agent1 -->|Query Data| MCPC\n    MCPC -->|Query Data| CDW\n\n    %% User Interaction Connections\n    Employee -->|Analytics| ClaudeDesktop\n\n    %% Styling\n    classDef external fill:#2196F3,stroke:#1565C0,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n    classDef user fill:#F5F5F5,stroke:#616161,stroke-width:3px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef nowassist fill:#FFB300,stroke:#F57F17,stroke-width:2px,color:#1a1a1a\n    classDef platform fill:#4CAF50,stroke:#2E7D32,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n    classDef wdf fill:#9C27B0,stroke:#6A1B9A,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff\n\n    class CDW external\n    class FinCase,FinVar platform\n    class Agent1 nowassist\n    class MCPS,MCPC wdf\n    class Employee,ClaudeDesktop user\n\n```\n\n> **Color Legend:** 🟡 Now Assist | 🟢 Platform | 🟣 Workflow Data Fabric | 🔵 External Systems | ⚪ User Interaction\n>\n> [📊 View High-Resolution Diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leojacinto/WorkflowDataFabric-TypeE/main/lab-guide/assets/dataflow_mcp.png)\n\n### MCP Client Configuration\n\n#### Hands-on: Configure MCP Client\n\nNavigate to AI Agent Studio Settings. Add a new MCP Server entry for Neon with API Key authentication.\n\n**Check the scope first.** The application scope (globe icon) decides where the MCP server, its alias and the agent copy are created. Click the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **globe icon** and make sure <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Forecast Variance** is selected. If it shows another scope, switch it before you continue. If the globe icon is not in the header (it moves once the Otto panel is on), use the header three-dot menu > **Scope selectors** > **Application scope**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_fund_exercise_scope.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n1. Navigate to All > type **AI Agent Studio**. On lab.service-now.com builds the left bar has **Manage MCP servers** as a menu entry that opens the list directly (or go to `/now/agent-studio/manage-mcp-servers`); in that case skip to step 2. Otherwise, in the left bar click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Settings** (gear icon). In the **Settings** page, expand <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Manage Model Contextual Protocol (MCP) Servers** and click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **View** next to **MCP servers**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_settings_mcp.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. The **Model Context Protocol Server** list opens. Click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **New**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_servers_list.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. In the **Add MCP Server** dialog enter the details below. On lab.service-now.com builds the dialog has two screens: **Name**, **Authentication type** (default **OAuth 2.1**, choose **API Key**) and **MCP server URL** first, then click **Next** and enter the **API Key**.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Name:** **Neon MCP Lab**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Authentication type:** **API Key**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **MCP server URL:** [**https://mcp.neon.tech/mcp**](https://mcp.neon.tech/mcp)\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark>**&#x20;API Key:** Bearer \\<ask\\_your\\_lab\\_guide\\_for\\_key>\n\nNote: there should be the word **Bearer** as a prefix so your value in the API Key will be something like **Bearer napi\\_some\\_secure\\_key**\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_server_add.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. Click **Add**. On lab.service-now.com builds two things can go wrong here. If a server with the same name already exists, the dialog fails with **Failed to create Connection Record using API key**: use a different name or remove the old one. After the server is created, open its connection (All > **Connections & Credentials** > **Connections** > the new Neon connection) and check **Connection URL**. It must read `https://mcp.neon.tech/mcp`; on the 7021 run it was saved as `https://mcp.neon.tech/` (the `/mcp` path was lost), and then adding the tool shows **Unable to fetch the tools for the MCP server**. Set the URL to `https://mcp.neon.tech/mcp` and click **Update**. The new server opens. If **Application** reads **Global**, the browser session was in Global scope: switch to **Forecast Variance** first and add the server again. Check that <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Application** reads **Forecast Variance** and that <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Tools** lists the Neon tools, such as **Add an OAuth provider** and **Compare database schema**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_server_created.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### AI Agent Configuration\n\n#### Hands-On: Configure new AI Agent for MCP scenario\n\nThis provides the steps needed to connect ServiceNow to an MCP ([Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/getting-started/intro)) Server tool configured in Neon. ServiceNow can serve as an MCP Client to connect to any solution that has MCP support.\n\nThis exercise does not cover the creation of the MCP Service from Neon as that requires administrator rights and CDW expertise which may not be widely available to various personas.\n\n1. Navigate to All > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> type **AI Agent Studio** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click on **Create and Manage**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_common_agent_studio_create_manage.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. Go to **AI agents** tab > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> click **Conditions** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> select **Field** as **Name** <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Operator** as **is** and for <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> Value type **Forecast Variance** (your agent is listed with your initials after the name) and hit **Return/Enter ↵**. Click on the <mark style=\"color:green;\">**e.)**</mark> result.\n\n   On lab.service-now.com builds the keyword search returns 0 rows and the agents have no initials. Use **Filter** > **Name** > **starts with** > **Forecast Variance** instead. Three agents are listed: **Forecast Variance**, **Forecast Variance Integration Hub Trigger** and **Forecast Variance Snowflake MCP**. Duplicate the one named exactly **Forecast Variance**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_agent_studio_search.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Click on **Forecast Variance \\<your initials>** (on lab.service-now.com builds: **Forecast Variance**).\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_zcc_forecast_variance_agent.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4.  Click on <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **more (vertical three dots)** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Duplicate**. On lab.service-now.com builds use the **Duplicate** icon at the right end of the agent's row in the list instead.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_duplicate_agent_menu.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n5.  You will get a prompt to confirm whether you want to duplicate the agent. Click **Duplicate**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_duplicate_confirm.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n6.  In the new Agent screen, go to the **AI agent name** and rename it to **Forecast Variance Neon MCP Lab**. On lab.service-now.com builds the copy opens in the setup wizard (**Define the specialty**, **Add tools and information**, **Define security controls**, **Add triggers**, **Select channels and status**), not on a canvas. A **Save updates?** dialog appears when you leave a step: confirm it. In **Define security controls**, user access shows **Allow if true** and data access **Dynamic user** with the approved role **admin**; if the role field is empty, add the role named exactly **admin**.\n\n    Scope: a duplicate made while the scope is **Global** lands in Global. Switch to **Forecast Variance** (header three-dot menu > **Scope selectors** > **Application scope**) before you duplicate.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_rename_agent_neon.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n#### Walkthrough: Complete AI Agent configuration\n\nAccept default security controls. Configure channels and status. Save and test.\n\n1.  On the specialty page click **Save and Continue**, then on the tools page click **Save and Continue** again without changing anything (you add the MCP step and tool in the next section). If a **Save updates?** dialog appears, click **Save updates**.\n\n2.  Since this is copied from an existing AI Agent configuration, simply accept the default values for **Define security controls** and its 2 sub-items. If **Define user access** shows **Users with specific roles** with an empty **Role(s)** field, type **admin** and pick it; **Save and continue** stays disabled until a role is set. Also keep A**dd triggers value** blank.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_security_defaults.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n3.  Finally, click on <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Select channels and status**. This configures the availability of the AI Agent. In this case, it is enabled and can be accessed using <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark>**&#x20;Now Assist panel** (named **Otto panel** on some instances) toggled on as well as via <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark>**&#x20;Now Assist in Virtual Agent** (named **Otto chat assistants** on some instances) added as chat assistant. Click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark>**&#x20;Save and test**. <mark style=\"color:$warning;\">**Note:**</mark> if Chat Assistants (step <mark style=\"color:green;\">**2.c.**</mark>) does not give you options, check and execute the steps in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub > Platform Configuration](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/main-exercises/lab-exercise-integration-hub#preparation-platform-configuration) > Steps 9 to 18; esp. if you are doing this lab standalone or have skipped the [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](https://servicenow-lf.gitbook.io/the-workflow-data-fabric-loom/main-exercises/lab-exercise-integration-hub) portion.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_channels_status_neon.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n4.  You **MIGHT** be alerted of potential duplicates but this is due to the multiple AI Agents created to test various integration scenarios. Click **Ignore and continue**.\n\n    <figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_duplicate_warning.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n5. Close the test tab. The copy is now saved and appears in the new AI Agent Studio.\n\n#### Hands-On: Configure MCP Step and Tool\n\nOpen the copy in the new AI Agent Studio. Add the MCP instructions to the agent. Add the Run SQL MCP server tool from Neon. Configure tool name, description, and execution mode.\n\n1. Navigate to All > type **AI Agent Studio** > click on **Agentic Solutions**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_agentic_solutions_nav.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n2. In the list, select the **AI agents** tab, type **Forecast Variance Neon MCP Lab** in **Search** and click the agent. The agent opens as a canvas. On lab.service-now.com builds, open the agent from **Create and manage** > **AI agents** instead and continue in the setup wizard; steps 3 to 10 below map to the wizard as follows.\n\n3. (Canvas builds) Click the **Edit** pencil on the agent in the middle of the canvas. The editor opens with the sections **Definitions, Tools, Access rules, Test scenarios, Triggers, Channels** and **Memories**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_agent_canvas_edit.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. In **Definitions > How-to instructions** (wizard builds: **Define the specialty**, scroll down to **List of steps**) go to **Step 2** (the agent you built in Integration Hub) and add one more bullet under it: **Also run the MCP tool \"Get Details via Neon MCP\" as a secondary check. Only return one entry (limit = 1). Columns should be \\[\"COST\\_CENTER\", \"ACTUAL\\_AMOUNT\\_USD\", \"BASELINE\\_AMOUNT\\_USD\", \"VARIANCE\", \"VARIANCE\\_PCT\"]**.\n\n5. Go to the **Tools** section (wizard builds: the **Add tools and information** page) and click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **+ Add tool** > <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Create new tool**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_add_tool_menu.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n6. In the list of tool types, click **MCP server tool**. A new tab **MCP server tool** opens next to the agent tab. On lab.service-now.com builds the menu is **Add tool** > **MCP server tool** and a dialog opens instead of a new tab.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_tool_type_menu.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n7. In the new tab, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> select **Neon MCP Lab** in **Select Model Context Protocol server**. A **Select tool** list appears and loads the tools of the Neon server (this can take a few seconds). Then <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> click **Select tool**, type **Run SQL** in **Search** and select **Run SQL** (not **Run SQL Transaction**). The **Inputs** list (sql, project\\_id, branch\\_id, database\\_name, role\\_name, compute\\_id, max\\_rows) appears. Leave the inputs empty.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_select_server_tool.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n8. Scroll down and provide the following details. You only need to modify three settings and leave the rest as they are.\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Name**: **Get Details via Neon MCP**\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Description for this AI agent**:\n\n* project\\_id: bitter-lab-28038915 (snake\\_case, not projectId)\n* sql: SELECT cost\\_center, actual\\_amount\\_usd, baseline\\_amount\\_usd, variance, variance\\_pct FROM \"VARIANCE\\_BASELINE\\_V\" WHERE cost\\_center = '\\{{cost\\_center\\}}' LIMIT 1\n\n<mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> **Execution mode**: **Autonomous**\n\n9. Click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**d.)**</mark> **Save** (top right of the tool tab). In the wizard dialog click **Add**; the tool then shows under **Model Context Protocol tools**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_tool_settings.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n10. Go back to the **agent tab** (first tab). The **Tools** section now lists **Get Details via Neon MCP**. Click **Save** (top right).\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_agent_tools_saved.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### AI Agent Testing\n\n#### Hands-on: Test and review Custom AI Agent\n\nEnter test prompt to process an expense event. Verify the MCP tool returns matching cost center data from Neon.\n\n**Before you test:** the test processes the event **EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01**, so that record has to exist. [Open the Expense Transaction Event list](/x_snc_forecast_v_0_expense_transaction_event_list.do) and look for it. If the list is empty, create it again with step 4 of **Hands-on: Flow Execution** in [Lab Exercise: Integration Hub](../main-exercises/lab-exercise-integration-hub.md); if the event is already there, skip that. Creating it fires the agent trigger, so a Finance Case can open from that run too. Each successful test run of the agent also opens one Finance Case through **Budget Variance Analysis**, so more than one case for CC\\_IT\\_001 is expected.\n\nIf the list shows **No records to display**, the event is missing.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_event_list_empty.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\nOnce the event exists, the list shows one row with Event ID **EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01** and cost center **CC\\_IT\\_001**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_event_list_row.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n1. In the new AI Agent Studio, open the agent canvas (All > AI Agent Studio > **Agentic Solutions** > **Forecast Variance Neon MCP Lab**) and click **Run test**. On lab.service-now.com builds there is no canvas or **Run test** dialog: go to AI Agent Studio > **Testing** > **Manual Test** > **AI agent or workflow**, pick **Forecast Variance Neon MCP Lab**, and send **Help me process EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01**. Turn on the Otto panel and activate the default assistant first (see **Preparation: Initial Checks** in the Integration Hub page), and create the two **Invoked from AI** ACLs from that page's platform preparation, or the run stops at **Access verification** with **Access denied**.\n\n2. In the **Run a test** dialog, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> keep **Single test** selected, <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> check that **Test scenario** shows **Help me process EXP-2025-IT-002-1007-01** (type it if it is empty) and <mark style=\"color:green;\">**c.)**</mark> click **Run single test**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_run_test_dialog.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. The **Trace log** opens on the right and runs the tools one after the other: **Extract Cost Center**, **Search for Cost Center History**, **Search for Expense Transactions History**, **Get Details via Neon MCP** and **Budget Variance Analysis**. Wait until the test shows <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **Completed**, then find <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> **Get Details via Neon MCP** in the list.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_aia_trace_log_result.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. Open the step **Get Details via Neon MCP** in the trace. It obtained the closest match for the value of cost center CC\\_IT\\_001. For this exercise, we only returned the raw JSON value to demonstrate the MCP capability where we did not use any SQL or API to return the matching row; instead we just provided a high-level instruction in Step 2 of the agent. **Budget Variance Analysis** also opens a Finance Case when the cost center is over budget, and its number is part of the final answer.\n\n#### If the test shows an error instead of results\n\nThe test chat may answer with this text instead of the review:\n\n> Sorry, there was a problem on my side trying to complete this request. Try asking again later.\n>\n> There are no agents available at the moment. Please try again later.\n\nSaving the agent in the new AI Agent Studio can clear its **Strategy**, and an agent without a Strategy cannot run. The new studio has no field for it, so you set it in the **AI Agents** list. The screenshots show the test agent of this lab; yours is named **Forecast Variance Neon MCP Lab**.\n\n1. Navigate to All, type **sn\\_aia\\_agent.list** and press **Enter**. The **AI Agents** list opens.\n\n2. In the **Name** search box type **Forecast Variance Neon MCP Lab** and press **Enter**. Look at the **Strategy** column of your agent. If it shows <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **(empty)**, continue. If it shows **ReAct**, the Strategy is not the cause of your error.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_fix_strategy_blank.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n3. Double-click the empty **Strategy** cell, type **ReAct**, select <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **ReAct** from the list and click <mark style=\"color:green;\">**b.)**</mark> the green check.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_fix_strategy_pick.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n4. The cell now shows <mark style=\"color:green;\">**a.)**</mark> **ReAct**. Go back to the agent in the new AI Agent Studio and click **Re-run test**.\n\n<figure><img src=\"../.gitbook/assets/sc_mcp_fix_strategy_saved.png\" alt=\"\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n### Conclusion\n\nCongratulations! You have created the **MCP Server** integrations that allows ServiceNow to make use of MCP capabilities from other systems outside ServiceNow, allowing LLM-powered integrations alternative to APIs that require less development.\n\n### Next step\n\nYou can explore a bonus use case that makes use of Stream Connect for Apache Kafka for integrations that require more throughput and data volume.\n\n[Take me back to main page](../)\n",
}
